1. ip link  => to list and modify interfaces in your host
2. ip a show dev <devname> => to list IPs assigned to a certain interface
3. telnet <host> <port> => to check if I can access a certain port in a certain host
4. host <hostname> => get ip of the host
5. host <ip> => get hostname of an IP
6. arp => address resolution protocal => to see mac address mapped to IP
7. ip i set up/down => to set interface up/down


Troubleshooting steps:
1. ip link => to see if the interface is already up 
2. nslookup => to check if the dns is working
3. traceroute <host> => to check the hop that has an issue
4. ss ( or netstat ) => to check ports a server is listening on



Ansible-Galaxies

1. ansible-galaxy collection --help
2. ansible-galaxy role --help
3. ansible-galaxy role init <rolename>
4. ansible-doc -l <collectionname> => to list all modules and plugins in a collection
5. ansibld-doc -l -t module <collectionname> => to list only modules in a collection